course: dictionary
lesson: 6694
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer chose. Occupied is a good example: it can mean busy, not free, or lived in.
explain: «The toilet is occupied.» Someone is using it right now, so it is not free. The clue is the sign on the door: a free toilet would be empty and ready.
explain: «Keep the children occupied» means give them something to do so they stay busy. The clue is keep, because you keep someone busy with a game or a task.
explain: In history, occupied means taken and controlled by an army. «Nazi Germany occupied Ukraine from 1941 to 1944.» The clue is that a country cannot be free when another country's army controls it.
fact: Occupied is the past form of the verb occupy. Occupy, occupies, occupied and occupying all come from the same word.
fact: As an adjective, «occupied» can mean being used by someone, not free: «an occupied seat».
fact: «Occupied» can also mean busy, or having your mind filled with something: «occupied with homework».
fact: «Occupied» can mean lived in: «an occupied house» has people living in it.
fact: «Occupied» can mean taken and controlled by an army or a group: «Large areas remain occupied.»
exercise: «The toilet is occupied.» What does occupied mean here? | Broken | *Someone is using it, so it is not free | Very clean | Empty and ready to use
exercise: Mum says, «I am occupied with my work.» What does occupied mean? | Lost | Lived in | *Busy, with my mind full of work | Free and relaxing
exercise: «Large areas in the east and south remain occupied.» What does occupied mean here? | Full of happy people | Painted bright colours | Shut for the night | *Taken and controlled by an army
test: «The seat is occupied, so please sit over there.» What is the opposite of occupied in this sentence? | *Empty | Full | Lived in | Busy
test: «Ella kept her little brother occupied with a puzzle.» What does occupied mean? | Made angry | Lost | *Kept busy | Taught to swim
exam: «The house was occupied by one family for years.» What does occupied mean? | Hidden | Sold cheaply | Painted | *Lived in
